## What becomes public

Each service has a public alias, such as `widget`. Everyone can list its tags,
image digest, supported platforms and publication/update timestamps. Choose
aliases and tags that you are willing to publish on an anonymous website.

Release Mirror preserves actual upstream tags. It does not invent versions,
turn builds into releases, fetch images, move registry tags or delete registry
objects. The producer decides when a successful build should appear.

This is a single-instance prototype. Live identity-provider setup, deployment
and hosted Renovate acceptance still need checking for each installation. See
the <%= link_to 'verification record', repository_file('docs/verification.md') %>
for the evidence and remaining limits.
